 # sds2-step-pipeline v5.4 — changes from the v4 candidate
 
+## v5.5w patch (sds2-weights-failures, on top of v5.4; same CLI, same outputs + manifest fields)
+
+- **Studs / rods / anchors / SDS2 bolt pieces are checked against SDS2's own weight.** `special_solid` builds them from
+  rings of mesh vertices or, failing that, a straight rod; v5.4 never compared the result with the piece weight. In the
+  data-3 family-weight jobs it wrote stud heads without shanks (EDWARDS AFB WS7/8 0.07 vs 1.04 lb), the first leg of
+  bent bars (Cats Rail RB1/2 0.18 vs 1.17 lb), curved rails as straight bars (SOCORRO RB1/2 0.72x) and rods 1/9 of
+  their weight. `turned_brep()`: when the primitive is a guess, or off SDS2's weight by more than 5 %, the piece's own
+  closed B-rep is used if it is within 15 % and closer (same weight gate as every exact piece). STERLING VIII RB3/4:
+  0.11x -> 1.0001x, all 101 bars exact.
+- **Ring detection no longer splits values on a .xxx5 boundary** (`_snap`): stations and radii were rounded to 3
+  decimals, so 0.4375 / 3.6875 split into two keys and rings were lost. Values within 0.002 in are now one cluster.
+- **Square / hex rings stay polygons** (`_polygon_ring`): bolt heads / nuts with exactly 4 or 6 vertices are the prism
+  of SDS2's own polygon, not a cylinder through its corners (+21 % on the head).
+- **Straight-rod stand-ins use the real diameter and length** (`rod_diameter`, `rod_length`): v5.4 used the piece-table
+  W field (not the diameter on 7.5+ jobs: RB3/4 W = 0.25) and L (the diameter on stud records: THD STUD 3/4 L = 0.75).
+  Now: the smallest extent of the piece's face vertices when the SDS2 name agrees (RB3/4, TWS2, THD STUD 3/4), and of
+  table L / vertex extent the one that reproduces SDS2's weight. Still tagged `[approx: straight rod ...]`.
+- **Special pieces built from their B-rep are no longer dropped** (`_absurd`): the shared-assembly tuple raised inside
+  `_absurd`, which counted as "absurd", so every such piece was skipped as `absurd_extent_corrupt_source_geometry`
+  (25 graded data-3 jobs; Eastwood 498 Heckmann anchors / DBA, TEMP JOB_RGK 2,511 RB bars).
+- **Job folders without the piece table (`subm/subm_idx`)** no longer fail stage 2 (FileNotFoundError -> fleet stage-1
+  fallback). Piece names, sections and weights exist only in that table, so members are written as tagged work-line
+  envelopes / joist stand-ins, SDS2 bolt records and reference parts as usual; the manifest carries
+  `counts.piece_table_absent` and `counts.subm_piece_files` and the class reason says the source file is missing.
+- **Weight tally split by geometry source**: `weight_check.by_source.{exact,built}` and `exact` / `built` parts in every
+  `by_family` entry (`exact` = SDS2's own piece B-rep, `built` = solids the converter built), `weight_check.turned_brep`.
+  SDS2's recorded weights differ from its own B-rep by fixed conventions (catalog lb/ft vs fillets sized from k_det;
+  AISC floor-plate psf for checkered plate; decks weighed as a 0.1 in sheet over the developed area), so only the
+  `built` part measures converter geometry (grading proposal in the agentjob README).
+
